* A byte immediate of an external in the immediate instructions (andi.b, to ccr, cmpi.b, and
* or.b to memory, which is ori.b) and a bit number (btst, bset): relocated as the whole extension
* word, R_68K_16, as both Microware assemblers do (linked: $FFFE for -2); before, R_68K_8 on its
* low byte ($00FE). move.b keeps the byte (R_68K_8 at 0x23).
* fixed: a0f6d83 2026-10-15 r68togas, l68, elf2mod: fixes from rebuilds of modules
* expect text: 023c0000 003c0000 02000000 0c2800000004 00100000 08000000 08e800000004 103c0000
* expect reloc: 00000002 R_68K_16          Ext_a
* expect reloc: 00000006 R_68K_16          Ext_a
* expect reloc: 0000000a R_68K_16          Ext_a
* expect reloc: 0000000e R_68K_16          Ext_a+0x00000001
* expect reloc: 00000014 R_68K_16          Ext_a
* expect reloc: 00000018 R_68K_16          Ext_a
* expect reloc: 0000001c R_68K_16          Ext_a
* expect reloc: 00000023 R_68K_8           Ext_a
 psect byte_imm_ext,0,0,0,0,0
 andi #Ext_a,ccr
 ori.b #Ext_a,ccr
 andi.b #Ext_a,d0
 cmpi.b #Ext_a+1,4(a0)
 or.b #Ext_a,(a0)
 btst #Ext_a,d0
 bset #Ext_a,4(a0)
 move.b #Ext_a,d0
 ends
